# Brand palette

When the user names a color, use this mapping. Do not invent extra oranges.

| They say | Token | Hex | Role |
|---|---|---|---|
| white, beige, beig, page | `page` | `#F6E6D0` | Page background |
| light brown, kraft | `kraft` | `#DFB88D` | Surfaces, cards |
| burgundy, burgandy, ink | `burgundy` | `#522028` | Type, primary buttons |
| copper | `copper` | `#962E17` | Warm accent, labels, errors |
| green, sage | `green` | `#5C6B4A` | Cool accent, muted text |
| gold | `gold` | `#EAB46F` | Highlight only, never on kraft |
| black, linework | `linework` | `#220A04` | Strokes, strongest marks |

Use the Tailwind tokens `bg-page`, `bg-kraft`, `text-burgundy`, `text-copper`, `text-green`, `bg-gold`, `text-linework`. Keep gold off kraft; it disappears.
